# Planning snapshot responsiveness verification

Read-only profiling of published revision 180: 1,666 nodes. No live store mutations, second harness, or provider calls.

| Phase | Before | After |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Snapshot disk load | 1,320 ms | 1,424 ms |
| Semantic preparation | 9 ms | 24 ms |
| Full candidate validation | 7,158 ms | 99 ms |
| Projection of all nodes | 2,732 ms | 12 ms |

The owner now prepares one immutable graph and indexes relations once per snapshot. Domain reference, prerequisite, parent-stage and review-blocking calculations reuse that index. Current-revision requests reuse the current in-memory snapshot, avoiding the disk-load phase. This preserves candidate immutability rather than dropping validation.

